Mon Oct 26 11:07:42 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.8.1 (upstream tag v0.8.1, 2026-10-25):
  * Security hardening: archive extraction, layout normalization and
    file enumeration hardened; release HTML URLs confined and
    browser-open links sanitized; decoded HTTP responses and
    screenshot decoding bounded; artifact URL identity bound in
    install and self-update; loopback bypasses the proxy and HTTP
    wire credentials are no longer logged; mutual challenge-response
    for single-instance IPC; local mirror reads bounded with
    deadlines and terminal escaping; remote feed overrides gated to
    dev builds.
  * Linux and FreeBSD install: pkexec and package tools are run from
    the system directories.
  * Settings: keep settings inside a portable suite; languages listed
    alphabetically by their own name; update check looks past a feed
    that is behind GitHub; one-time notice that closing the window
    keeps the launcher in the tray.
  * UI: maximized title bar close button takes the screen corner;
    wgpu limits capped to what the GPU offers; non-UTF-8 arguments
    ignored; busy state cleared when a worker panics.
  * Windows: version-folder wrapped portable ZIPs install, pinned
    taskbar icons survive updates; macOS: quitting no longer crashes
    and Intel Macs skip wgpu indirect-call validation; FreeBSD
    aarch64 cross build packaged.
  * Re-vendored: shipped target only gets version bumps (cc,
    ordered-float, smallvec, uuid, ...); the new craft-quit
    (MIT OR Apache-2.0, storytold/craft-libs) only does something on
    macOS. Licence set unchanged, no new system deps.
- Refresh artcraft-launcher-pkcon-first.patch for the 0.8.1 sources:
  upstream now runs pkexec and package tools from the system
  directories, so pkcon is looked up and run the same way
  (system_tool) instead of through PATH; PR
  storytold/craft-launcher#256 still open
- Set the metainfo release date to 2026-10-25

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 23 06:52:22 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.7.0 (upstream tag v0.7.0, 2026-10-23):
  * Security hardening: release/feed download URLs confined to the
    app's repository and the artifact version bound to the release;
    a tarball whose app binary is a symlink is refused before any
    chmod; single-instance replace authenticated and the local
    mirror server bounded; shell metacharacters rejected in opened
    web links; decoded feed size, screenshot dimensions and locale
    tags bounded. No CVE ids assigned.
  * Date/time conversion goes through jiff instead of hand-rolled
    calendar code.
  * Windows: self-update and portable version checks run without
    PowerShell and install only files signed like the launcher;
    busy download renames retried, Windows Installer runs logged.
  * 0.6.1: saved filters no longer hide every app on startup;
    clearer update dialog (Download case) and AppImage folder
    wording; FreeBSD aarch64 installs its own tarball.
  * Re-vendored: shipped target only gets version bumps (icu_* 2.4.0,
    ureq 3.5.0, webbrowser 1.2.5, zerovec 0.11.9, ...); the new
    verifysign (BSD-3-Clause) and winsafe (MIT) are Windows-only.
    Licence set unchanged (MPL-2.0 option-ext 0.2.0, Unlicense ksni
    0.3.7), no new system deps, MSRV unchanged; cargo_audit clean.
- Rebase artcraft-launcher-pkcon-first.patch for the 0.7.0 sources
  (line offsets only, content unchanged; PR
  storytold/craft-launcher#256 still open)
- Set the metainfo release date to 2026-10-23 (it still said
  2026-10-18 from 0.5.1) and name ksni 0.3.7, the vendored version
  since 0.6.0, in the Legal-Review-Notice

