Mon Oct 12 18:25:32 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package artcraft-launcher 0.3.2 (upstream tag v0.3.2, 2026-10-11):
  * One place to find, install, update and open the 12-app Craft suite
    (PhotoCraft, LightCraft, FilmCraft, DesignCraft, VectorCraft,
    PdfCraft, EffectCraft, WordCraft, DeckCraft, GridCraft, CADCraft
    and SoundCraft), with the right build picked for your computer.
  * Handles distro packages (deb/rpm/tar), Flatpak bundles and AppImage
    installs, serializes queued installs, and filters detection by arch.
  * Lives in the system tray (ksni StatusNotifierItem, no GTK needed),
    tells you when updates are ready, and updates itself.
  * License derived over the vendor tree for the shipped desktop target:
    MPL-2.0 (option-ext via dirs), Unlicense (ksni), ISC, BSD-2/3-Clause,
    Zlib, Unicode-3.0, CC-BY-4.0/CC0-1.0 social icons, OFL-1.1 fonts and
    Ubuntu-font-1.0, see the Legal-Review-Notice in the spec; docs/brand
    (trademarked) stays in the sources unmodified as compile-time input
    only (five files embedded by include_image!/include_bytes!) and is
    never installed.
  * No CLI binary ships, so no -cli subpackage split. No CVEs known.
- Add artcraft-launcher-pkcon-first.patch: Linux install/update/remove go through PackageKit when the distro carries the app (storytold/craft-launcher#256, open), download flow stays as fallback
- Recommend PackageKit for the new path

